msgid "FIG-24 describes the WUT-only reference, separate from the explicitly selected [finite SRAM4 copy](u575-stop2-copy.md) in FIG-27. It separates the independent RTC domain from the drained RUN domain. Solid arrows name current calls, admission or cleanup transitions; dashed arrows name external source premises and exits outside this WUT-only scope. Hardware drain does not repair a tainted clock. The separately selected Stop2 owner supplies WUT and restoration; the read-only clock component alone supplies neither. No arrow establishes physical residency or automatic enrollment."
msgstr "FIG-24 describes the WUT-only reference, separate from the explicitly selected [finite SRAM4 copy](u575-stop2-copy.md) in FIG-27. It separates the independent RTC domain from the drained RUN domain. Solid arrows name current calls, admission or cleanup transitions; dashed arrows name external source premises and exits outside this WUT-only scope. Hardware drain does not repair a tainted clock. The separately selected Stop2 owner supplies WUT and restoration; the read-only clock component alone supplies neither. No arrow establishes physical residency or automatic enrollment."

msgid "The separate [single-tuple LPTIM1 LPBAM selection](u575-lptim1-lpbam.md) uses the ordinary retained-clock initializer with `wake_owner=nx_stm32u575_stop2_identity()`, the same concrete Stop2 owner and no AlarmA-copy opt-in. Its public receiver start/stop owns LPTIM1 access preparation and restoration; a partial start failure retains its effects until joined stop proves their release. This does not change the read-only clock contract or the WUT-only scope of FIG-24."
msgstr "The separate [single-tuple LPTIM1 LPBAM selection](u575-lptim1-lpbam.md) uses the ordinary retained-clock initializer with `wake_owner=nx_stm32u575_stop2_identity()`, the same concrete Stop2 owner and no AlarmA-copy opt-in. Its public receiver start/stop owns LPTIM1 access preparation and restoration; a partial start failure retains its effects until joined stop proves their release. This does not change the read-only clock contract or the WUT-only scope of FIG-24."

